{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:22:02Z","created_by_operation":"op_cf928ab885564331944d343cbffb8706","id":"pg_58f3ec439e2c52b89e70f4094df5d2fc","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/nano-collective-nanocoder-readme-zh-cn-md-0cb0afb026ef-f4094df5d2fc.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_ec67b8e4b0665d52bb76e74f433a21b5"],"title":"Nano-Collective/nanocoder/README.zh-CN.md @ 0cb0afb026ef","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:22:02Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cf928ab885564331944d343cbffb8706"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0715cc6329213e55f2e1d03b6342c2fbcc8a4afca6a270b14c5eede9410d3c69"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A starting development mode can be selected at launch via --mode; documented examples include yolo and plan modes."},{"claim_ids":["clm_531f376dbad83d0cc191fdb0cecddc3f0eaf0505704832b1ac1578f717ef87d3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Two rendering modes exist: a fullscreen alternate-screen layout with in-app scrolling (default, with a --mouse toggle) and an inline mode via --no-alt-screen or an \"alternateScreen\": false preference that prints into the terminal's native scrollback."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6c5797fb6476e38bb5902669a8714e99dfcbced31260c20a754a8531d4e1a297"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the README directs contributors to CONTRIBUTING.md for development setup and guidelines, and notes shared conventions, tests, and release standards across Nano Collective projects."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c6fe79bbc9dcfc62600f9109ca921e0529d802a4e30a427bb689801bd1ca7162"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI accepts --provider and --model flags in both interactive form and with a non-interactive 'run' subcommand, and flags may appear before or after the run subcommand."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0715cc6329213e55f2e1d03b6342c2fbcc8a4afca6a270b14c5eede9410d3c69","clm_531f376dbad83d0cc191fdb0cecddc3f0eaf0505704832b1ac1578f717ef87d3","clm_6c5797fb6476e38bb5902669a8714e99dfcbced31260c20a754a8531d4e1a297","clm_c6fe79bbc9dcfc62600f9109ca921e0529d802a4e30a427bb689801bd1ca7162"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:22:02Z","created_by_operation":"op_cf928ab885564331944d343cbffb8706","id":"pg_68c59e95ff435abc9e117335cdd86b3d","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/nano-collective-nanocoder-readme-md-0cb0afb026ef-7335cdd86b3d.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_a5125e44f98f5207a7b8f974963aeac4"],"title":"Nano-Collective/nanocoder/README.md @ 0cb0afb026ef","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:22:02Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cf928ab885564331944d343cbffb8706"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_05adf1dbd5acc75a3ba51bffc8cfb4f07e4c07f801645595fc3e82a593b95ca5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Tool calling uses three paths: native function calling plus XML and JSON fallbacks, with malformed-output repair on both fallback paths so weaker or non-conforming models still work end to end."},{"claim_ids":["clm_31c2f30736151c5c29b14451ea58282c1f34b0e1b5ed5db46f4193309f006ba0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A per-project daemon ('nanocoder daemon start') owns file-watch and cron event sources, letting Skills subscribe to file.changed or schedule.cron events and run headless without the TUI; launchd plist and systemd user-unit installers ship in-tree."},{"claim_ids":["clm_480bb4483b59ecd8f3f493b55e2845d1169cb1af32b4ebc759139612b4e030e4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project's own comparison doc acknowledges being behind peers in community size, surface breadth (no desktop or web app), extension depth relative to Pi, IDE-level code intelligence (LSP client only, no debugger integration), and distribution polish."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6bf53e54f33c3a9316354f670cf4bf87d52e19c91cb99c39e9a9eda248cc2b34"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The cron-driven scheduler is documented as powered by the croner library."},{"claim_ids":["clm_873b896b0447d5efebc617f6830390d175fce36af2e3cea7443697f22e23b3fc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent supports 20+ providers: native cloud integrations (e.g. Anthropic, OpenAI, Google Gemini, OpenRouter, Copilot, Mistral, Z.ai), seven documented local servers (Ollama, llama.cpp, llama-swap, LM Studio, LocalAI, MLX Server, vLLM), and any custom OpenAI-compatible endpoint."},{"claim_ids":["clm_97479ad2a9c88ee3de0902260f1a81ed1753c63e9308e3d10d2b43133089d323"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Nanocoder can run as an Agent Client Protocol agent via 'nanocoder --acp', exposing conversation, tool-calling, and permission flows to ACP-compatible editors such as Zed."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cccb0f6569f54d2856c1eef97db14aa5f0b59343e7526222882d431d4e560744"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Stated design principles are zero telemetry, zero tracking, and local-first operation, with the whole loop able to run on-machine against local models with no outbound network traffic."}],"claim_ids":["clm_05adf1dbd5acc75a3ba51bffc8cfb4f07e4c07f801645595fc3e82a593b95ca5","clm_31c2f30736151c5c29b14451ea58282c1f34b0e1b5ed5db46f4193309f006ba0","clm_480bb4483b59ecd8f3f493b55e2845d1169cb1af32b4ebc759139612b4e030e4","clm_6bf53e54f33c3a9316354f670cf4bf87d52e19c91cb99c39e9a9eda248cc2b34","clm_873b896b0447d5efebc617f6830390d175fce36af2e3cea7443697f22e23b3fc","clm_97479ad2a9c88ee3de0902260f1a81ed1753c63e9308e3d10d2b43133089d323","clm_cccb0f6569f54d2856c1eef97db14aa5f0b59343e7526222882d431d4e560744"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:22:02Z","created_by_operation":"op_cf928ab885564331944d343cbffb8706","id":"pg_b5fa8af522f8575d92b4fbc752b1094b","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/nano-collective-nanocoder-docs-battlemap-md-0cb0afb026ef-fbc752b1094b.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_9d6ce2b11e9f516b8dc7c2b85a6877b0"],"title":"Nano-Collective/nanocoder/docs/battlemap.md @ 0cb0afb026ef","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:22:02Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cf928ab885564331944d343cbffb8706"}
